A||N||1||Jonathan||Won't start, please help!||||13||
Z||000000||Jonathan||04-27-2001||06:58 AM||||Hope you can point me in the right direction here.  My Fiero will not start.  (V6)Recently it was having intermittent problems with smoking and lurching.  Now it has just stopped running.  I replaced all of my ignition components.  New pickup coil, new ignition module, and new coil.  (Some of these were still under warranty from the last time I had trouble.)  I put everything back together, and still had nothing, no spark at all.  I checked the wire between the coil and module, it was ok.  I tried it without the tach filter plugged in.  I know I am getting gas, and also know I am not getting any spark.  So....wait a minute.  Oops, I didn't pay atention to the orientation of the rotor button when I removed/reinstalled the distributor.  Removed #1 spark plug, got the the cylinder to TDC, and the reinstalled the distributor so that the rotor pointed to the #1 terminal.  Still nothing.  <P>Any ideas on where to go from here.  Starting to get frustrated.....I want to drive my Fiero again.  Been down for a while now.  <P>Thanks for your help,<P>Jonathan||||reg||13
Z||000001||Bluemagic||04-27-2001||09:15 AM||||I had the same problem turned out to be the fuel pump was not maintaining the fuel pressure of 45 psi also make sure the pickup in the distributor is not rusted,wish you luck. ||||reg||14
